  data: {
    LLM: "1. Foundation Building: Move any available Ace to a foundation slot. Build up on it in the same suit (2, 3, 4...).\n2. Tableau Building: You may move a card onto another card in the tableau if it is exactly one rank lower and of the SAME SUIT (e.g., 9 of Hearts onto 10 of Hearts).\n3. Reserves: Any exposed card can be moved to an empty Free Cell. Only one card per cell.\n4. Moving Sequences: You can move a correctly ordered suit-sequence if you have enough empty cells to 'shuttle' the cards. Movement is limited to (Empty Cells + 1).",
    Player: "1. Foundation Building: Move any available Ace to a foundation slot. Build up on it in the same suit (2, 3, 4...).\n2. Tableau Building: You may move a card onto another card in the tableau if it is exactly one rank lower and of the SAME SUIT (e.g., 9 of Hearts onto 10 of Hearts).\n3. Reserves: Any exposed card can be moved to an empty Free Cell. Only one card per cell.\n4. Moving Sequences: You can move a correctly ordered suit-sequence if you have enough empty cells to 'shuttle' the cards. Movement is limited to (Empty Cells + 1).",
    objective: 'Move all 52 cards to the four foundation piles, organized by suit from Ace up to King.',
    gameplay: "1. Foundation Building: Move any available Ace to a foundation slot. Build up on it in the same suit (2, 3, 4...).\n2. Tableau Building: You may move a card onto another card in the tableau if it is exactly one rank lower and of the SAME SUIT (e.g., 9 of Hearts onto 10 of Hearts).\n3. Reserves: Any exposed card can be moved to an empty Free Cell. Only one card per cell.\n4. Moving Sequences: You can move a correctly ordered suit-sequence if you have enough empty cells to 'shuttle' the cards. Movement is limited to (Empty Cells + 1).",
    keyRules: [
      'Only KINGS (or sequences starting with a King) can be moved into an empty tableau column.',
      'Building is strictly SAME SUIT (unlike FreeCell which is alternating colors).',
      'Cells can be used for any card rank.',
